```console
$ um workflow run resume --help
Continue a local workflow run, or a Cloud run with --cloud

Usage: um workflow run resume [OPTIONS] <RUN>

Arguments:
  <RUN>  Run directory, or the id or subject of a run under the um home

Options:
      --from <STEP>                    Ordinary step to reexecute (repeatable); without it, resume a waiting or abandoned run
      --workflow <FILE>                Replacement workflow file within the run's original source root
      --execution-root <PATH>          Existing execution root; defaults to the previous attempt's root
      --plain                          Force plain human presentation
      --json                           Print the workflow result as JSON
      --color <WHEN>                   Select renderer color behavior [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
      --cloud <ORGANIZATION>           Act in Cloud in this organization (ID or exact slug) instead of locally
      --service-api-key-file <PATH|->  Authenticate with a service API key from a private file, or - for standard input
      --allow-insecure-http            Allow this command's Useful Machinery requests over insecure HTTP connections
  -h, --help                           Print help

Select one or more ordinary steps with --from. Their downstream ordinary dependents run again; other eligible ordinary steps are inherited. Every finalizer runs again. The original run inputs and Git baseline remain authoritative.

Without --from, a waiting run continues once a control resolves its wait and otherwise reports the wait unchanged, and a run whose process died continues from the step it was running.

With --cloud ORGANIZATION, RUN is a Cloud run ID: the command asks Cloud to continue that run under its own definition from the steps --from names, or with none from where its record stands, and reports the request as um run continue does. It reads and writes no local run.

```
